        }
      ],
      "message": "scalar: Force inlining of 4x64 mul_512 and reduce_512\n\nWithout inlining, GCC generates slower code for the 128-bit accumulator\nin secp256k1_scalar_mul_512, depending on details such as how the\naccumulator is updated in the extract macro. With both functions\ninlined into secp256k1_scalar_mul, GCC generates the same code\nindependently of these details. Clang benefits from scheduling across\nthe boundary between multiplication and reduction.\n\nIn a scalar_mul latency benchmark (bench_internal) on an Alder Lake\nP-core, this is 4% faster with GCC and 10% faster with Clang.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Tim Ruffing",
        "email": "me@real-or-random.org",
        "date": "2026-10-01T13:41:19Z"
      },
