      "message": "scalar: Eliminate c2 and use 128-bit accumulator in 4x64 reduce_512\n\nIn secp256k1_scalar_reduce_512, all limb multiplications involve either\nSECP256K1_N_C_0 (0x402da1732fc9bebf) or SECP256K1_N_C_1 (0x551231950b75fc44).\nBoth constants are strictly < 2^63, and SECP256K1_N_C_0 + SECP256K1_N_C_1\nis ~0.58 * 2^64.\n\nConsequently, the accumulator peaks at ~0.58 * 2^128 and never overflows\n128 bits under any 512-bit input. The third limb c2 is therefore never\nincremented.\n\nSwitching all accumulator calls in reduce_512 to the _fast variants\n(muladd_fast, sumadd_fast, extract_fast) allows eliminating c2 from\nreduce_512 entirely. Furthermore, the unused sumadd macro is removed.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Yudistira Putra",
        "email": "85178972+Yudis-bit@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-03T23:06:17Z"
